  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Prime Minister Narendra Modi recently engaged in a series of public events during the Diwali holiday, focusing on national security and tribal welfare. While visiting Central Reserve Police Force personnel in Bastar, he characterized ideological supporters of Naxalism as a threat to the Constitution and called for their identification. Concurrently, he participated in a virtual program for 'Janjatiya Gaurav Diwas,' marking the 151st birth anniversary of tribal freedom fighter Birsa Munda. During these events, he asserted that tribal populations were historically neglected and denied democratic rights due to Maoist violence under previous governments. These statements were met with criticism from the Indian National Congress, whose leadership labeled the rhetoric as divisive. The Prime Minister's remarks coincide with a broader period of political discourse, including recent tributes paid to former Prime Minister Jawaharlal Nehru on his birth anniversary and ongoing discussions regarding international residency status for prominent figures.",
